course: dictionary
lesson: 3255
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary gives each meaning a number, and you choose the one that fits the sentence. Episode has two main meanings: one part of a TV show, radio show, podcast or story told in parts, and one event or short period of time that stands out.
explain: «In every episode of Tom and Jerry, a grey cat crashes round a big kitchen after a cheeky mouse.» The clues are «Tom and Jerry» and the cat chasing a mouse, which are parts of a cartoon show. So here episode means one part of a show. Always ask: what kind of episode is this?
explain: Now try the second meaning. «She had an episode of illness last winter» means a short period when she was ill, a time that stood out from her normal life. Read a little further than the word itself, because the words around it tell you which meaning is right.
fact: An episode is one part of a TV or radio series, a podcast, or a story told in parts.
fact: An episode can also be one event or short period of time that stands out, like an episode of illness.
fact: Useful phrases are «the next episode», «the first episode», «an episode of» and «a funny episode».
fact: A cliffhanger ends a chapter or episode at a tense moment, so the reader must read on.
fact: Streaming plays the next episode automatically; turning off autoplay helps you decide when to stop.
exercise: In «The first episode ends with a cliffhanger.», what does episode mean? | *One part of a TV show or story told in parts | A kind of cliff | A party for the whole class | One event or short period of time that stands out
exercise: «She had an episode of illness last winter.» What does episode mean here? | *A short period of illness that stood out | A kitchen cupboard | One part of a TV series | A funny story about a cat
exercise: «Turning off autoplay helps you decide when to stop watching the next episode.» Why is this useful? | *You choose when to stop, not the screen | It makes the next episode start faster | It stops the cat from crashing | It makes the screen brighter
test: «The reader wanted to know what happened next, because the episode ended with a cliffhanger.» What does episode mean? | An illness that lasts a long time | A type of cliff | A room in a house | *One part of a story told in parts
test: Which clue in «In every episode of Tom and Jerry, a grey cat crashes round a big kitchen» shows that episode means a part of a show? | crashes | *Tom and Jerry | grey | kitchen
exam: In «It cannot see the future, so it invents next week's episode.», what does episode most likely mean? | A short time of heavy snow | A kind of invention | *One part of a series, like next week's show | A word for the future
